# Member Session Portal Authority (PCMS-001)

**Principle:** Member identity (`atour_mb_session`) is owned by **`apps/portal` only** (cookie **write**). Marketing may **read** the shared cookie for header chrome and PDP CTA shaping, and may **host** the shared OTP/profile UI via a Portal-origin `GuestAuthTransport` (Phase 5 — §5.5). Marketing must not write the cookie or expose member BFF routes (`app/api/me/*` / `app/api/public-auth/*`). Operator uses `atour_op_session` on `apps/web` — separate actor.

---

## 1. Surfaces

| Surface | Session | Registration auth |
| ------- | ------- | ----------------- |
| Marketing | Read-only SSR probe (`readMarketingMemberSessionFromCookies`) for header chrome **and** PDP CTA shaping | **Guest PDP (Phase 6):** «ثبت‌نام» and «ورود» open the **marketing** login modal (Portal-origin OTP). JS `preventDefault` — stay on `/tours/{id}` even when the origin transport is missing (show `BACKEND_UNREACHABLE` in the dialog). `href` is **no-JS only** (portal `/catalog/{id}/register`, optional `?auth=login` on «ورود»). **Logged-in PDP:** hide `[data-marketing-tour-sign-in]`; continue → `/catalog/{id}/register` (no `auth=login`, no modal). **Already-registered self:** primary → `/me/registrations/{id}` (`[data-marketing-view-registration]`). **Header Sign in** navigates to Portal `/login?portalReturn=/me/registrations` (**page** phone/OTP/profile — **not** a portal modal, **not** the marketing modal). Authenticated header → profile chip via `resolveMarketingMemberHeader`. Future marketing login hosts may reuse the PDP modal; header stays a page egress until product asks. |
| Portal | `atour_mb_session` read/write | **`/login`:** page phone/OTP/profile (`data-portal-login-full-page` — **not** a portal modal). **Register guests:** OTP in the **register-only** login modal (PCMS-UX-MODAL-04). Session members: tour intake full-page on `/catalog/{id}/register`. |
| Web admin | `atour_op_session` | Operator invite login — never member cookie |

---

## 2. Registration resume (PCMS-REG-01)

When a member with valid portal cookie opens `/catalog/{tourId}/register`:

1. Server reads `readPublicCatalogSessionFromCookies()`
2. Session `tenantId` must match `resolvePortalBootstrapForHost(host).tenantId`
3. Server prefetches member profile via allowlisted `fetchMemberProfileFromSession` (same upstream as profile BFF) when session cookie is present → initial flow step **`intake`**
4. **Stepper (PCMS-REG-02):** Resume at intake uses stepper mode **`intake-only`** — single «ثبت‌نام» step; auth steps (phone/otp/profile) are **not** shown as complete (they were skipped via session, not traversed in this flow).
5. When SSR cannot read `Domain=<apex>` cookies (dev Playwright custom apex), client flow hydrates from `/api/me/profile` and sets `data-registration-resume="intake"` on the flow root
6. No marketing changes required

Custom apex dev smoke (`portal.denali.club`) does not resolve in Node DNS — SSR profile prefetch must not call `http://portal.denali.club:3003/...` directly. Use `PORTAL_INTERNAL_URL` (default dev `http://127.0.0.1:3003`) and forward ingress via **`x-forwarded-host`** (not HTTP `Host` — undici overwrites loopback Host) so tenant bind resolves tenant `…000003`.

OTP remains mandatory for guests without valid member session.

---

## 3. Tenant bind (PCMS-SEC-01)

When portal bootstrap resolves `tenantId` for host:

- Member JWT `tenant_id` **must** match (fail-closed)
- Mismatch → clear `atour_mb_session` + redirect/`401`
- When bootstrap + dev host map both fail to resolve tenant: **fail-closed in production** (`failClosedWhenUnresolved`); dev may remain permissive for IP staging

### JWT verify (PCMS-SEC-02)

Portal middleware and `readPublicCatalogSessionFromCookies` use `validateSessionTokenAsync`:

1. Decode claims (`sub`, `tenant_id`, `exp`, `sess_ver`)
2. When `AUTH_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY` + issuer/audience configured → **RS256 signature verify** (Edge Web Crypto)
3. Reject forgeries with `invalid_signature` → clear cookie on protected paths

Full `sess_ver` vs DB membership version remains **API authority** on BFF upstream calls (`AUTH_TOKEN_REVOKED`). Middleware signature verify closes the forge gap; revoke is enforced on `/api/*` and `/api/me/*` upstream.

When `AUTH_JWT_*` unset (unit tests / legacy dev), decode-only fallback remains for velocity. **Dev Cloud / agent-start** must still copy `AUTH_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY` + issuer/audience from API into portal (and marketing/web) `.env.local` so Edge verify is on — otherwise a decode-valid JWT with a dead membership still enters `/me/*`.

### Dead member session fail-close (PCMS-SEC-03 — 2026-08-18)

JWT decode in middleware is **not** proof the member still exists in identity. Portal `/me/*` SSR must treat same-origin `GET /api/me/profile` **401/403/404** (and coded `AUTH_TOKEN_REVOKED` / `UNAUTHORIZED_INVALID_BEARER_TOKEN` / `AUTH_UNAUTHENTICATED`) as a **dead session**:

1. Do **not** render `PortalMemberShell` with fallback chip «عضو» / `loadFailed` while nav stays live
2. Clear `atour_mb_session` via `clearSessionCookieOnResponse` (host-only **and** `Domain=<share-parent>` — PCMS-COOK-04)
3. Redirect to **`/login?portalReturn=<safe /me path>`** (PCMS-03) — **not** marketing, **not** HTTP 501

Egress lives on `GET /api/public-auth/expire-session` so Set-Cookie clear can attach to the redirect. `/me/layout` and `/me/profile` call this when `fetchMemberProfile` classifies the BFF failure as `unauthenticated`. `/me/layout` also uses the same egress when session decode is `null` or JWT `tenant_id` ≠ portal bootstrap — **never** `redirect("/")` (portal `/` bounces toward marketing without clearing `atour_mb_session`).

**Do not** fail-close **502** / `BACKEND_UNREACHABLE` / network errors — those are outages; keep `loadFailed` on the profile page and do not wipe the cookie.

`buildMemberApiHeaders` must read the session token from the **same** source as `readPublicCatalogSessionFromCookies` (`cookies()` then raw `Cookie` header). Header-only fallback with no `Authorization` Bearer produces a ghost shell (session valid, profile 401).

Middleware on protected `/me/*` tenant mismatch must **`redirectToMemberLogin` + clear cookie** — not `redirectHome` to `/`. Unauthenticated `/me/*` fallback path is `/login?portalReturn=…`, never `/`.

Entitlements BFF **401/403** must **not** fall back to `evaluateMemberPortalEntitlements` (that kept live nav without identity). Empty `granted`, **not cacheable**. **502** / network may still use the local SDK shim.

---

## 4. Cookie domain (PCMS-COOK-01)

Default: **host-only** (no `Domain=` attribute) on legacy platform portal ingress `{club}.portal.{root}` (e.g. `denali.portal.localhost`) and non-apex platform hosts.

**PCMS-COOK-02 (dev):** Bare `Domain=localhost` or `Domain=.localhost` is **rejected** by Chromium (`localhost` is on the Public Suffix List) — never emit those Domain attributes. Auth BFF may still write **host-only** cookies on legacy `{club}.portal.localhost`.

**PCMS-COOK-03 (shared Domain — custom apex + localhost inverted portal):** Portal sets / refreshes `atour_mb_session` with `Domain=<share-parent>` via `resolveMemberSessionCookieDomain` / `shouldRefreshDevMemberSessionCookieDomain` / `setSessionCookieOnResponse(..., "shared")` when ingress is:

| Ingress | Cookie `Domain=` | Marketing sibling that receives cookie |
| ------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| `portal.{apex}` (custom apex, e.g. `portal.denali.club`) | `{apex}` (`denali.club`) | `{apex}` |
| `portal.{club}.localhost` (canonical local portal) | `{club}.localhost` (`denali.localhost`) | `{club}.localhost` |

**Logic:** Chromium accepts `Domain=denali.localhost` from host `portal.denali.localhost` (parent of both portal and marketing). It **rejects** the same Domain from legacy `denali.portal.localhost` (not a subdomain of `denali.localhost`). Therefore local M↔P header chrome requires the **prod-shaped** portal host `portal.{club}.localhost` — `buildDevPortalPublicBaseUrl` emits that shape when `PLATFORM_ROOT_DOMAIN=localhost`.

**PCMS-COOK-05 (legacy localhost portal → canonical — 2026-07-17):** When `PLATFORM_ROOT_DOMAIN` is `localhost` (or unset → `localhost`), Portal middleware **must** 308-redirect legacy platform portal hosts `{club}.portal.localhost` (any port) to canonical `portal.{club}.localhost` **before** JWT validation, auth redirects, or cookie refresh. Scope is localhost-only — custom apex and non-localhost `{club}.portal.{root}` are not rewritten. Redirect preserves pathname, query, protocol, and port; uses HTTP **308** so POST auth BFF routes (including `/api/public-auth/*`) keep their method. Parsing uses `toCanonicalClubPortalHost` / `parseMultiLevelTenantHost` (exact shape match; fail-closed; no string replace). After redirect, session writes occur on the inverted host and receive `Domain={club}.localhost` (PCMS-COOK-03), so Marketing `{club}.localhost` can read `atour_mb_session`. Legacy remains temporarily accepted only as a redirect source.

**PCMS-COOK-04 (logout clear):** `clearSessionCookieOnResponse` emits **two** `Set-Cookie` clears when a shared Domain applies — host-only **and** `Domain=<share-parent>` — so marketing loses the session when portal logout runs. Legacy `{club}.portal.localhost` emits host-only clear only (pre-redirect / residual host-only jars).

**Marketing probe (PCMS-03-READ):** `readMarketingMemberSessionFromCookies` mirrors portal cookie read — `cookies()` first, then raw `Cookie` header via `readSessionTokenFromCookieHeader`. `resolveMarketingMemberHeader` binds session `tenant_id` to marketing bootstrap **or** dev host map (`marketing` / `portal` surface) before rendering the profile chip.

**PCMS-03-DEV (cross-surface tenant bind):** When `ALLOW_DEV_WEB_SESSION=true` and ingress is `*.localhost`, `sessionTenantMatchesDevCrossSurfaceHost` accepts a valid member session when its `tenant_id` matches the paired M+P dev host map for the session's club label — even if marketing bootstrap fell back to `TOUR_OPS_DEV_TENANT_ID` on an unmapped host (e.g. bare `localhost:3002`). Production remains strict: widened branch is gated by `isDevGuestHostAllowed()`.

When ingress is custom apex (`tryParseCustomApexHost`) or inverted localhost portal (`portal.{club}.localhost` → `club_portal`), portal sets `Domain=<share-parent>` on `Set-Cookie` / clear so member session is shared with the marketing sibling for that tenant only.

Cookie write points: `verify-otp` (returning member), `register-complete` (new guest after profile), `/api/me/mobile/verify`, logout clear.

**Never** platform-wide `Domain=.platform-root` or `Domain=.localhost`. Derivation is host-based at cookie write time — no `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` env.

---

## 5. Marketing portal link (PCMS-03)

Marketing header **Sign in** (`data-marketing-header-sign-in`) must target member **OTP login**, not a protected `/me/*` route directly. Guests hitting `/me/*` without `atour_mb_session` previously bounced to portal `/` then marketing — a redirect loop.

### 5.0 Sign-in egress (PCMS-03 login — 2026-07-14)

| Actor | Builder | Target |
| ----- | ------- | ------ |
| Marketing header Sign in | `resolvePortalMemberLoginUrl(host)` | Portal `/login?portalReturn=/me/registrations` (**page** phone/OTP/profile; no auto-modal) |
| Marketing tour PDP «ورود برای ادامه ثبت‌نام» | `resolvePortalRegistrationLoginUrl(host, tourId)` | **Href fallback** only: Portal `/catalog/{tourId}/register?auth=login`. **JS:** marketing modal stays on `/tours/{id}` (PCMS-MKT-AUTH-05). |
| Portal register guest (any visit) | Auto `openLoginModal` (PCMS-UX-MODAL-04) | Modal over register; `?auth=login` remains a compatible deep link / reopen |
| Portal register reopen after dismiss | `PortalRegisterSignInLink` → `openLoginModal` | Same-page modal; no navigate-away |
| Marketing footer «ثبت‌نام‌های من» | `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl(host)` | Portal `/me/registrations` (middleware redirects guests to `/login?portalReturn=…`) |
| Portal middleware (unauthenticated `/me/*`) | `resolvePortalMemberLoginPath(host, returnPath)` | `/login?portalReturn=<requested /me/* path>` |

**Login presentation (PCMS-UX-MODAL — 2026-07-16, amended DL-48):** Register-guest OTP is a **portal-hosted modal** (desktop dialog · mobile bottom sheet). Standalone `/login` is **page** OTP, not that modal. Design SoT: [portal-member-login-modal.mdoc](../phase-19/portal-member-login-modal.mdoc) · DL-40 · DL-48.

| Host | Role |
| ---- | ---- |
| `/login` | **Page-level public host (DL-48)** — required for middleware `/me/*` gate (guests never render `/me` React). Marker `data-portal-login-full-page`. Phone / OTP / profile run **on the page** (`[data-portal-login-form-panel]` + `PublicCatalogRegistrationFlow` with `memberLoginEgress`). **Do not** open `PortalLoginModalProvider` on this route (`host="login"` is deleted). Host `onAuthenticated` → `completeMemberLoginEgress`. Shared steps still use `GuestAuthTransport` (no fetch URLs in Layer A). |
| `/catalog/{id}/register` | Full tour **intake** page. Guests **must** complete member auth in the **register-only** login modal first (**PCMS-UX-MODAL-04**). The modal has no login-host egress (`completeMemberLoginEgress` lives on the `/login` page host). Session members land intake-only (PCMS-REG-01). Intake stays on the page, never inside the modal. |

**Login route (PCMS-03-LOGIN):** Deep link **`/login`** remains canonical for standalone sign-in and `/me` redirects. OTP steps are shared with catalog registration auth steps (`memberLoginEgress`); smoke tour id bootstraps the flow plugin server-side only. Legacy `/catalog/{id}/register?portalReturn=…` redirects to `/login?portalReturn=…`.

**Login tour id (smoke-tour bootstrap, not a catalog page):** `resolveMemberLoginCatalogTourId(pluginId)` — workspace smoke map (Denali dev `…0220`, operator `…0210`, …). Override: `PORTAL_MEMBER_LOGIN_TOUR_ID` / `PORTAL_DEV_GUEST_TOUR_ID`. The id is passed into the page flow plugin as `tourId` context only. `fetchCatalogTour` may supply a title; a missing row **must not** `notFound()` the `/login` host. The page must not render tour intake or tour price. Story copy + OTP form on the same page is allowed (existing `data-portal-login-full-page` skin).

**Post-OTP return:**

| Invariant | Rule |
| --------- | ---- |
| **PCMS-UX-01** | `GET /login` without safe `portalReturn` → SSR redirect to canonical `/login?portalReturn=<default member module>`. |
| **PCMS-UX-02** | Valid member session on `/login` → redirect to `portalReturn` (**no** OTP page/modal). Register `?auth=login` with session → intake-only (no modal). |
| **PCMS-UX-03** | After `verify-otp` / `register-complete` on **login-host** egress: auth steps call `GuestAuthTransport.probeSession()` then host `onAuthenticated` → `completeMemberLoginEgress()` / `location.assign(portalReturn)`. **`hydrateCatalogRegistrationIntakeAfterSession` is forbidden** on login-host egress **and** inside OTP/profile steps. |
| **PCMS-UX-04** | `data-portal-return` (host or modal root) mirrors query for client fallback. |
| **PCMS-UX-MODAL-01** | Desktop = dialog · mobile = bottom sheet · hooks `data-portal-login-modal` / `data-portal-login-modal-presentation`. |
| **PCMS-UX-MODAL-02** | While modal open on register host: stay on URL; close without success keeps the page. |
| **PCMS-UX-MODAL-03** | Register-host modal success: cookie probe → close modal → intake-only on **page** (not intake in modal). |
| **PCMS-UX-MODAL-04** | **Modal-first tour register (2026-08-05):** Guest on `/catalog/{id}/register` (no valid member session for host tenant) **must not** render inline phone/OTP/profile on the page. Auto-open login modal (same as `?auth=login`). New members: display name **required**, email **optional** (`register-complete`). Close without success keeps the register URL; page shows auth gate + reopen control — **no** tour intake until session. |
| **PCMS-UX-MODAL-COOKIE** | Every modal success path must probe same-origin session (`waitForMemberSessionCookie`) so the session cookie is committed and COOK-03 can refresh `Domain=<share-parent>` on **custom apex** or **`portal.{club}.localhost`** — otherwise marketing SSR cannot detect the member. Legacy `{club}.portal.localhost` probe still avoids login redirect loops but does not share with marketing. |

**Login chrome (PCMS-03-UX):** `/login` page uses login titles (`loginPageTitle`) and marketing back where applicable — **no** registration stepper chrome (`memberLoginEgress`). Auth still runs phone → OTP → (profile if new). The **register** host keeps the shared login **modal** (PCMS-UX-MODAL-04). That modal is register-only: no `host="login"` branch, no `onLoginSessionReady`.

**Portal modal hygiene (1.5.3):** `PortalLoginModalProvider` always presents `data-portal-login-modal-host="register"`. Callers pass `{ flow }` (optional `portalReturn`); they do not choose a host. Marketing `MarketingLoginModalContext` must **not** expose `canHostAuth` — a missing origin transport still `preventDefault`s and opens the dialog (PCMS-MKT-AUTH-05).

**Register route (tour registration):** `/catalog/{tourId}/register` is **intake-first after auth**. Guests are gated by PCMS-UX-MODAL-04 (modal OTP / profile). Session resume → intake-only (PCMS-REG-01). Inline guest auth on the register page is **forbidden**.

**Auth API (unchanged contract):** `phone-preflight` → `request-otp` → `verify-otp` (existing member → session) **or** `requires_registration` → profile → `register-complete` (new member → session). Portal BFF under `/api/public-auth/*`.

**GuestAuthTransport (Phase 1 — multi-host-capable):** Shared OTP/profile steps in `@app-tour/catalog-registration-flow-ui` must not `fetch` BFF paths or `location.assign`. They read `GuestAuthHost` (`transport` + `onAuthenticated`) from `GuestAuthHostProvider`. Transport methods: `preflightPhone` → `{ exists }`; `requestOtp` → `{ challengeId }`; `verifyOtp` → `{ outcome: "session_ready" } | { outcome: "needs_profile", onboardingToken }`; `completeProfile` → `{ outcome: "session_ready" }`; `probeSession` → `{ ready }` (PCMS-UX-MODAL-COOKIE). After `session_ready`, steps call `probeSession` then host `onAuthenticated` only — they must not hydrate intake, read `portalReturn`, or `location.assign`.

Two factories (do **not** merge; do **not** add `baseUrl` to the Portal factory):

| Factory | Host | Network | `probeSession` |
| ------- | ---- | ------- | -------------- |
| `createPortalSameOriginGuestAuthTransport()` (arity 0) | Portal only | Relative `/api/public-auth/*` | `waitForMemberSessionCookie` → `GET /api/me/profile` |
| `tryCreatePortalOriginGuestAuthTransport(portalPublicBaseUrl)` / `createPortalOriginGuestAuthTransport` | Marketing (Phase 5) | Absolute `{portalOrigin}/api/public-auth/*` with `credentials: "include"` | `GET {portalOrigin}/api/public-auth/session` → `{ ok, ready }` |

Cookie `Set-Cookie` remains Portal BFF. Adapters **must not** persist JSON `session_token`. **Phase 4 (PCMS-CORS-01):** CORS on Portal `/api/public-auth/*` only — see §5.4. **Phase 5 (§5.5):** Marketing **may** host the same OTP/profile UI via the origin factory. Marketing still **must not** write `atour_mb_session`, expose `app/api/me/*` / `app/api/public-auth/*`, CORS `/api/me/*`, rewrite OTP/profile UI, create `packages/guest-auth`, move session ownership, or delete `/login`.

**Cross-intent after login:** Marketing **header** Sign in navigates to Portal `/login` (page OTP). Guest PDP `[data-marketing-register]` (primaryKind `register`) and `[data-marketing-tour-sign-in]` open the **marketing** modal; after OTP, marketing **reloads** the current URL so SSR chrome/CTA can see the cookie. Member `[data-marketing-register]` (primaryKind `continue` / register-another) navigates to portal `/catalog/{id}/register` for **intake**. Portal `/login` remains the `/me/*` middleware gate.

### 5.2 Marketing authenticated header (PCMS-03 — 2026-07-14)

Marketing **SSR** must detect portal members via the shared cookie (read-only). This is mandatory for header chrome after modal login on portal:

1. `readMarketingMemberSessionFromCookies` — JWT validate (PCMS-SEC-02).
2. `resolveMarketingMemberHeader(host, tenantId)` — tenant bind (PCMS-03-DEV / SEC-01) + `GET /identity/me` for display/avatar.
3. Shell: profile chip (`data-marketing-header-member`) **or** Sign in (`data-marketing-header-sign-in`).
4. Root: `data-marketing-member-authenticated` when member.

Marketing must **not** write member cookies or expose member BFF routes — cookie probe stays in `read-marketing-member-session.server.ts`. Phase 5 (§5.5) **does** host OTP UI on marketing via Portal-origin `fetch`; that UI must not call `GET /api/me/profile` or write `atour_mb_session`. The same SSR probe still feeds PDP CTA shaping (§5.3); it does not create a second session authority.

After portal modal login on **custom apex** or **`portal.{club}.localhost`**, PCMS-UX-MODAL-COOKIE + COOK-03 (`Domain=<share-parent>`) ensure the next marketing SSR request can see `atour_mb_session`. Legacy `{club}.portal.localhost` does not share with `{club}.localhost`. `*.localhost` marketing often cannot read a host-only portal cookie — fail-closed to guest CTAs is expected in that topology.

### 5.3 Marketing PDP CTA matrix (Phase 3 — 2026-08-16)

Tour detail (`/tours/{tourId}`) must not keep asking a signed-in member to «ورود» or to «ثبت‌نام» as if they had no self booking.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  READ[readMarketingMemberSessionFromCookies]
  BIND[sessionTenantMatchesDevCrossSurfaceHost]
  READ -->|null / invalid JWT| GUEST[Guest CTA: register + sign-in]
  READ -->|valid JWT| BIND
  BIND -->|mismatch| GUEST
  BIND -->|match| FORT[tryResolveCatalogRegistrationForTourApiPath]
  FORT -->|no manifest path| CONT[Member-continue: register, hide sign-in]
  FORT -->|path| API["GET API /{ws}/registrations/for-tour/{tourId}<br/>Bearer + x-user-id"]
  API -->|error / self null| CONT
  API -->|self.id| VIEW["Member-self: view /me/registrations/id<br/>optional register-another"]
```

| Layer | File | Role |
| ----- | ---- | ---- |
| Cookie read | `read-marketing-member-session.server.ts` | Same PCMS-03-READ probe as header |
| CTA pure matrix | `resolve-marketing-tour-detail-cta.ts` | Guest / member-continue / member-self hrefs — no fetch |
| For-tour SSR | `fetch-marketing-member-self-registration-for-tour.server.ts` | API + Bearer; never portal `/api/me/*` |
| Path map | `tryResolveCatalogRegistrationForTourApiPath` | Manifest `GET /{ws}/registrations/for-tour/:tourId` → `/{ws}/registrations` (Denali only on trunk) |
| Detail URL | `resolveWebMemberRegistrationDetailUrl` | GSH `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl(host)` + `/{id}` (no open redirect) |
| Presentation | `catalog-tour-detail-register-cta.tsx` | Shared by rail + sticky; sold-out still yields view-self when a self id exists |

**Why not portal BFF from marketing?** Calling `portal.{host}/api/me/registrations/for-tour` from marketing Node would either use the public portal origin (cookie not sent cross-origin; custom apex DNS may not resolve in SSR) or invent a marketing `/api/me/*` proxy — both violate PCMS (no marketing member BFF). Header chrome already calls API `GET /identity/me` with Bearer; for-tour is the same pattern on a member-gated workspace route.

**Why a generated path map instead of `resolveCatalogRegistrationApiPath`?** That resolver throws unless a workspace intake plugin is **registered** at runtime. Marketing must not static-import `@app-tour/workspace-*` or bootstrap intake plugins (ADR-MKT-004 / MKT-6). Catalog list already uses generated `WORKSPACE_CATALOG_LIST_PATHS`; for-tour follows the same codegen (workspaces without the route are omitted — Urban/Harbor/guest-club stay member-continue).

Workspaces without `selfRegistrationGate` / for-tour **must not** be special-cased by `pluginId === "denali"` in `apps/marketing`.

Hooks: `[data-marketing-register]` (SMK-MKT-03, guest + continue + register-another) · `[data-marketing-tour-sign-in]` (**guest only**) · `[data-marketing-view-registration]` (member-self primary) · `[data-marketing-register-another]` (member-self secondary) · `[data-marketing-tour-detail-cta-mode]`.

**Default module route:** Resolved from workspace `memberPortal.defaultPrimaryModuleId` (Denali Phase 2: `trips` → `/me/registrations`). The path `/me/registrations` remains a **permanent alias** independent of default (DL-03).

### 5.4 Marketing → Portal public-auth CORS (Phase 4 — 2026-08-16)

Architect YES (Phase 4) unlocked **browser credentialed `fetch` from the paired marketing origin to Portal `/api/public-auth/*`**. Cookie write, tenant bind, and `/login` stay on Portal. Phase 5 (§5.5) uses this CORS door for the Marketing Portal-origin adapter — it does **not** expand CORS onto `/api/me/*`.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  REQ["Browser Origin + Portal Host"]
  GSH["resolvePublicAuthCorsAllowOrigin"]
  REQ --> GSH
  GSH -->|"origin missing / invalid / other club / admin / api"| NONE["No ACAO — fail-closed"]
  GSH -->|"origin ∈ {portal public origin, paired marketing origin}"| ACAO["ACAO = exact origin + credentials"]
  ACAO --> PATH{"pathname /api/public-auth/* ?"}
  PATH -->|no| STRIP["Do not attach CORS — /api/me/* pages GSH stay same-origin"]
  PATH -->|yes| HDR["Allow-Methods GET POST OPTIONS · Allow-Headers content-type"]
```

| Invariant | Rule |
| --------- | ---- |
| **PCMS-CORS-01** | CORS headers exist **only** on Portal `/api/public-auth/*` (middleware). Never `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`. Never CORS `/api/me/*`, catalog BFF, or `apps/api` `/public/auth/*` (API stays server-to-server). |
| **PCMS-CORS-02** | Allow origin is the request `Origin` **iff** it equals `new URL(resolvePortalPublicBaseUrl(host)).origin` **or** `new URL(resolveMarketingPublicBaseUrl(host)).origin`. Cross-club, admin, operator web, and arbitrary origins get **no** ACAO (OPTIONS → 403). |
| **PCMS-CORS-03** | Credentialed: `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` with the echoed origin. `Set-Cookie` on `verify-otp` / `register-complete` / logout **still** uses Portal BFF + COOK-03 Domain helpers — Marketing must not persist `session_token` from JSON. |
| **PCMS-CORS-04** | OPTIONS preflight short-circuits in middleware (204 + CORS when allowed). No COOK-03 refresh on OPTIONS. |
| **PCMS-CORS-05** | `GET /api/public-auth/session` → `{ ok: true, ready: boolean }` after JWT validate + portal tenant bind. No profile PII, no token. Phase 5 Portal-origin `probeSession` must use this path — **not** CORS on `GET /api/me/profile` (`waitForMemberSessionCookie` stays Portal same-origin). |

**Why not CORS `/api/me/*`?** Member profile/registrations BFF is portal-private. A marketing OTP host only needs public-auth (phone → OTP → profile complete) plus a boolean cookie probe. Expanding CORS to `/api/me/*` would leak member APIs to any allowed marketing origin script.

**Why CORS before the Marketing host?** Layer A UI + `tryCreatePortalOriginGuestAuthTransport` are Phase 5 (§5.5). Phase 4 only opened the network door so that factory can `fetch(portalOrigin + "/api/public-auth/…", { credentials: "include" })` without a PCMS waiver.

**Same-site vs host-only:** Custom apex + `portal.{club}.localhost` still rely on COOK-03 `Domain=<share-parent>` so marketing SSR can read the cookie after a CORS OTP. `*.localhost` marketing often cannot see a host-only portal cookie — fail-closed guest CTAs remain expected.

### 5.5 Marketing Portal-origin auth host (Phase 5 — 2026-08-16)

Marketing becomes a **second auth UI host**, but only where staying on the tour page matters. Cookie write stays Portal BFF. The shared phone/OTP/profile steps stay in `@app-tour/catalog-registration-flow-ui`. Marketing must **not** mount `PublicCatalogRegistrationFlow` (that host hydrates intake and `GET /api/me/profile`).

**Surface split (2026-08-16, 1.5.1 / Phase 6 2026-08-17):** The marketing modal is the **PDP** guest auth host («ثبت‌نام» + «ورود»). Header `[data-marketing-header-sign-in]` is **not** a modal trigger — it is a real navigation to Portal `/login` (PCMS-03 / §5.0). `MarketingLoginModalProvider` stays in the marketing layout so PDP (and a future marketing login host) can open the dialog without a second provider tree.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  HEADER["Header Sign in"]
  PDP["PDP guest register + ورود"]
  LOGIN["Portal /login page OTP"]
  MODAL["Marketing login modal · catalogRegistrationAuthFlowSteps"]
  ORIGIN["tryCreatePortalOriginGuestAuthTransport"]
  CORS["Portal /api/public-auth/* + CORS"]
  COOKIE["Set-Cookie atour_mb_session · COOK-03"]
  PROBE["GET portalOrigin/api/public-auth/session"]
  RELOAD["window.location reload current marketing URL"]
  SSR["Next marketing SSR · header chip + PDP CTA"]
  HEADER --> LOGIN
  PDP --> MODAL
  MODAL --> ORIGIN
  ORIGIN --> CORS
  CORS --> COOKIE
  ORIGIN --> PROBE
  PROBE --> RELOAD
  RELOAD --> SSR
```

| Invariant | Rule |
| --------- | ---- |
| **PCMS-MKT-AUTH-01** | `tryCreatePortalOriginGuestAuthTransport(portalPublicBaseUrl)` parses `http(s)` origin only (no `*`, no userinfo, no relative). Invalid → `null`. `createPortalOriginGuestAuthTransport` throws `GuestAuthTransportError("network")` on invalid. Do **not** add `baseUrl` to `createPortalSameOriginGuestAuthTransport` (arity 0, Portal-only). |
| **PCMS-MKT-AUTH-02** | Origin adapter POSTs `{origin}/api/public-auth/{phone-preflight,request-otp,verify-otp,register-complete}` with `credentials: "include"`. Ignore JSON `session_token` — never persist it. |
| **PCMS-MKT-AUTH-03** | Origin `probeSession` retries `GET {origin}/api/public-auth/session` until `{ ok: true, ready: true }` (bounded, same anti-hang budget as `waitForMemberSessionCookie`). **Zero** `GET /api/me/profile` from marketing. After `session_ready` from verify/register-complete, auth steps **always** call host `onAuthenticated` even when the probe returns `ready: false` **or throws** (network / AbortError / 3PCD). Wrap the probe in its own try; do not skip `onAuthenticated` from the probe catch. Chromium Tracking Protection (3PCD) treats `fetch` from `{club}.localhost` to `portal.{club}.localhost` as third-party, so the session GET may not see `Domain={club}.localhost` while the cookie is already in the jar for the first-party marketing reload. Blocking on `!ready` or a thrown probe leaves the OTP modal stuck (SMK-MKT-03). |
| **PCMS-MKT-AUTH-04** | Marketing modal uses `GuestAuthHostProvider` + `catalogRegistrationAuthFlowSteps` with `memberLoginEgress: true`. Host `onAuthenticated` reloads the **current marketing URL** (strip `auth=login` if present). Not `completeMemberLoginEgress`, not intake hydrate. |
| **PCMS-MKT-AUTH-05** | **Header** `[data-marketing-header-sign-in]` is a plain `<a href={resolvePortalMemberLoginUrl}>` — full navigation to Portal `/login` (no `preventDefault`, no marketing modal). **PDP guest** `[data-marketing-register]` (primaryKind `register`) and `[data-marketing-tour-sign-in]` use `MarketingLoginModalTrigger` with client `preventDefault` whenever `MarketingLoginModalProvider` is mounted so the guest **stays on `/tours/{id}`**. Missing origin transport still opens the dialog and shows `catalogRegistration.errors.BACKEND_UNREACHABLE` — do **not** navigate to portal register with JS. `href` is no-JS / no-provider only (`/catalog/{id}/register` on «ثبت‌نام»; `register?auth=login` on «ورود»). Do **not** put `canHostAuth` on the public modal context (that invites a trigger to skip `preventDefault`). Transport null is an internal render branch (`[data-marketing-login-unavailable]`). Optional marketing `?auth=login` auto-opens the modal **only** on a tour-detail pathname (including when transport is null). `host="header"` on the marketing modal is reserved for a future marketing login surface — do not wire the chrome Sign in to it. |
| **PCMS-MKT-AUTH-06** | Member `[data-marketing-register]` (primaryKind `continue` / `register-another`) **navigates** to portal `/catalog/{id}/register` for intake. Guest primaryKind `register` must **not**. Portal `/login` is **not** deleted. No `apps/marketing/app/api/public-auth/*`, no `app/api/me/*`, no cookie Domain helper changes. Intake never mounts on marketing. |

**Why reload instead of client hydrate?** Marketing header chip and PDP CTA matrix are **SSR** (PCMS-03 / §5.3). After CORS `Set-Cookie` on the Portal host, the next marketing document request is what COOK-03 sharing is designed for. Client-only state would lie on `*.localhost` host-only cookies.

**Why a second factory?** Portal same-origin `probeSession` must keep using `/api/me/profile` (no CORS on `/api/me/*`). Marketing must use the boolean public-auth session probe. Sharing one `baseUrl` argument would tempt `/api/me/profile` across origin.

### 5.1 PCMS-003 Phase 3 follow-up — applied (2026-07-05)

| Field | Value |
| ----- | ----- |
| **Trigger** | `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl` merged in GSH + delegation live |
| **PCMS-003 update** | Marketing footer / nav member-module links use registry default module URL; header Sign in uses `resolvePortalMemberLoginUrl` (2026-07-14) |
| **Traceability** | DL-22 · DL-26 · [builder-migration-contract.mdoc](../phase-19/member-portal-shell/builder-migration-contract.mdoc) · `guard-member-url-builder` |
| **Cleanup** | Marketing migrated to `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl` (PS-7 prep); remove deprecated export in BP-8 |

